---
import PageFrame from "../components/PageFrame.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Logos AI Pricing"
  description="A simple three-lane pricing model for Logos AI: Free, BYOK, and Managed."
>
  <PageFrame current="pricing">
    <main class="shell py-16">
      <section class="max-w-4xl animate-rise">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 section-title">Free to start. Paid when convenience removes friction.</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 section-copy">
          Keep pricing easy to understand: a meaningful free core, BYOK for power users, and a managed plan for people
          who want setup removed and the whole thing working out of the box.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-muted">Free</p>
          <div class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl text-text">$0</div>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Bible reading, lightweight browser demo, app download, limited study help, and a credible first experience.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
            <li>Meaningful reading experience</li>
            <li>Downloadable desktop app</li>
            <li>Basic usage without friction</li>
            <li>Enough value to build trust</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="surface-card border-accent/40 bg-accent/5 p-8">
          <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-accent">Bring Your Own Key</p>
          <div class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl text-text">Control</div>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Already have an API key? Plug it in and unlock advanced features on your terms without forcing Logos AI to
            absorb the whole usage bill.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
            <li>No Logos AI monthly fee for the core BYOK path</li>
            <li>Best fit for technical users</li>
            <li>Advanced users keep provider-level control</li>
            <li>Strong zero-cost path for power usage</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="surface-card border-gold/40 bg-gold/5 p-8">
          <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-gold">Managed</p>
          <div class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl text-text">$5-$15</div>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Let Logos AI handle setup, hosting, and convenience for you. This is the main monetization path.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
            <li>Instant AI access</li>
            <li>No API key setup</li>
            <li>Premium voices and saved history</li>
            <li>Priority usage and richer commentary tools</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow">Future Packs</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-text">Sell accelerators, not ransom.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Premium upgrades should make serious users faster, not make the free product feel fake. Good candidates:
            sermon prep, original languages, premium voices, church tools, and export-heavy workflows.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow">Messaging Rule</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-text">Do not complain about costs.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Lead with choice and convenience instead. "Use your own API key, or let Logos AI handle everything for you"
            is strong positioning. "I need to charge because APIs cost money" is weak positioning.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </PageFrame>
</SiteLayout>
